WEBVTT

1
00:00:57.333 --> 00:01:01.541


2
00:01:01.541 --> 00:01:03.541
<b>Duryodhana says, </b>

3
00:01:03.541 --> 00:01:06.833
<b>"O best of the Brahmins (Acharya), </b>

4
00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:12.541
<b>now understand the key warriors in our army. </b>

5
00:01:12.541 --> 00:01:17.583
<b>I shall inform you about</b>
<b>the captains of my army</b>

6
00:01:17.583 --> 00:01:18.958
<b>There are yourself,</b>

7
00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:20.500
<b>Dronacharya,</b>

8
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.708
<b>and Grandsire Bhishma, </b>

9
00:01:22.708 --> 00:01:28.458
<b>Karna, and the ever-victorious</b>
<b>Kripacharya in battle. </b>

10
00:01:28.458 --> 00:01:33.833
<b>There are also Ashvatthama, Vikarna,</b>
<b>and the son of Somadatta. </b>

11
00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:41.291
<b>Many other mighty warriors are ready to</b>
<b>lay down their lives for my sake. </b>

12
00:01:41.291 --> 00:01:46.958
<b>They are all skilled in various weapons</b>
<b>and experienced in warfare."</b>

13
00:01:47.625 --> 00:01:51.541


14
00:01:51.541 --> 00:01:52.791
<b>Now here, </b>

15
00:01:52.791 --> 00:01:58.500
<b>Duryodhana is boosting the morale</b>
<b>of the Kaurava warriors by naming them.</b>

16
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:02.916
<b>It's as if he's saying, </b>

17
00:02:02.916 --> 00:02:05.750
<b>We are even mightier than them. </b>

18
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.833
<b>Do we have any less heroes?" </b>

19
00:02:08.833 --> 00:02:15.750
<b>By naming the warriors on his side, he wants to</b>
<b>make them all feel highly distinguished.</b>

20
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:16.750
<b>However, </b>

21
00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:21.416
<b>he has addressed Guru Drona here with</b>
<b>a double-edged sword. </b>

22
00:02:21.416 --> 00:02:24.625
<b>By placing his name before Grandsire Bhishma, </b>

23
00:02:24.625 --> 00:02:31.833
<b>he first shows respect, but then a slight sarcasm </b>
<b>by calling him the best of the Brahmins</b>

24
00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:35.416
<b>Guru Drona is not a Kshatriya,</b>
<b>but a Brahmin </b>

25
00:02:35.416 --> 00:02:40.458
<b>who teaches military education in the classroom,</b>
<b>not on the battlefield. </b>

26
00:02:40.458 --> 00:02:42.708
<b>It's as if Duryodhana is saying,</b>

27
00:02:42.708 --> 00:02:47.166
<b>"Guru Drona, don't remain</b>
<b>soft-hearted like Brahmins. </b>

28
00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:52.125
<b>When you get the opportunity</b>
<b>to fight alongside Kshatriyas, fight like a warrior."</b>

29
00:02:52.125 --> 00:02:54.833
<b>Duryodhana, skilled in diplomacy, </b>

30
00:02:54.833 --> 00:02:58.000
<b>has carefully chosen some names. </b>

31
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.958
<b>For instance, among his brothers,</b>
<b>he names Vikarna,</b>

32
00:03:01.958 --> 00:03:03.375
<b> not Dushasana. </b>

33
00:03:03.375 --> 00:03:05.750
<b>Dushasana would support him anyway. </b>

34
00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.750
<b>But Vikarna? </b>

35
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.041
<b>Vikarna had opposed the disrobing of Draupadi. </b>

36
00:03:12.041 --> 00:03:12.958
<b>Therefore,</b>

37
00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:19.375
<b>it was crucial to make Vikarna feel special</b>

38
00:03:19.375 --> 00:03:20.375
<b>In the end, </b>

39
00:03:20.375 --> 00:03:27.500
<b>without naming any specific person,</b>
<b>Duryodhana addresses all the mighty warriors, </b>

40
00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.166
<b>saying they are all skilled in warfare</b>

41
00:03:30.166 --> 00:03:33.875
<b>and none of them will hesitate</b>

42
00:03:33.875 --> 00:03:38.125
<b>By doing so, he is honoring them all,</b>

43
00:03:38.125 --> 00:03:39.000
<b>but </b>

44
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.375
<b>at the same time, he is also binding them </b>

45
00:03:42.375 --> 00:03:46.125
<b>to fight with full glory.</b>

46
00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.875
<b>It's also interesting </b>

47
00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:51.125
<b>to note that he mentions Karna here, </b>

48
00:03:51.125 --> 00:03:54.041
<b>who is not even present on the battlefield. </b>

49
00:03:54.041 --> 00:03:55.500
<b>Karna had vowed, </b>

50
00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:02.208
<b>that as long as Bhishma was leading the </b>
<b>Kauravas,Karna will not to participate in the war.</b>

51
00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:06.375
<b>We will further understand this in more detail.</b>

52
00:04:06.916 --> 00:04:11.583


53
00:04:11.583 --> 00:04:14.541
<b>Duryodhana and Karna are close friends, </b>

54
00:04:14.541 --> 00:04:15.958
<b>and that's why</b>

55
00:04:15.958 --> 00:04:22.875
<b>Karna's name was mentioned despite</b>
<b>his absence from the battlefield. </b>

56
00:04:22.875 --> 00:04:28.916
<b>This is the only name Duryodhana took,</b>
<b>swayed by his feelings for his friend.</b>

57
00:04:28.916 --> 00:04:31.166
<b>Karna had vowed </b>

58
00:04:31.166 --> 00:04:36.583
<b>not to set foot in this war while </b>
<b>Grandsire Bhishma was present. </b>

59
00:04:36.583 --> 00:04:43.041
<b>So, taking his name in front of everyone</b>
<b>disrespects Grandsire Bhishma, doesn't it?</b>

60
00:04:43.041 --> 00:04:47.666
<b>Both Karna and Grandsire Bhishma</b>

61
00:04:47.666 --> 00:04:48.833
<b>But</b>

62
00:04:48.833 --> 00:04:50.416
<b>by getting carried away with emotions, </b>

63
00:04:50.416 --> 00:04:54.250
<b>it's wrong to disregard Grandsire Bhishma. </b>

64
00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:58.750
<b>After all, he is also supporting Duryodhana.</b>

65
00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:01.166
<b>It often happens </b>

66
00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:05.291
<b>that two of our friends don't get along. </b>

67
00:05:05.291 --> 00:05:07.958
<b>And we, siding with one, </b>

68
00:05:07.958 --> 00:05:11.125
<b>consider the other bad</b>

69
00:05:11.125 --> 00:05:13.750
<b>and speak ill of them. </b>

70
00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.666
<b>We should understand </b>

71
00:05:15.666 --> 00:05:19.708
<b>that there must be valid reasons for their dispute, </b>

72
00:05:19.708 --> 00:05:21.208
<b>but for us, </b>

73
00:05:21.208 --> 00:05:26.791
<b>both of their love is equal, right?</b>

74
00:05:26.791 --> 00:05:29.833
<b>Whether their views match or not, </b>

75
00:05:29.833 --> 00:05:33.000
<b>it's more important to think </b>

76
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:36.541
<b>about how much they love us. </b>

77
00:05:36.541 --> 00:05:42.625
<b>Only by viewing all relationships independently</b>
<b>can a balance be maintained.</b>

78
00:05:43.125 --> 00:05:46.875
<b> </b>

79
00:05:46.875 --> 00:05:53.125
<b>While one should not hesitate to</b>
<b>support a friend or family member, </b>

80
00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:54.375
<b>But then, </b>

81
00:05:54.375 --> 00:05:57.416
<b>standing by them in unrighteousness? </b>

82
00:05:57.416 --> 00:06:00.333
<b>is it even a right thing to do?</b>

83
00:06:00.333 --> 00:06:04.791
<b>By doing so, you not only encourage</b>
<b>their distorted thoughts</b>

84
00:06:04.791 --> 00:06:05.791
<b>but also</b>

85
00:06:05.791 --> 00:06:10.750
<b>become a partner in sin.</b>

86
00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:12.416
<b>All the kings   </b>

87
00:06:12.416 --> 00:06:15.375
<b>who supported Duryodhana </b>

88
00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:18.708
<b>also supported unrighteousness. </b>

89
00:06:18.708 --> 00:06:20.500
<b>Some of them</b>

90
00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:24.000
<b>were as self-interested as Duryodhana; </b>

91
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.666
<b>their end was certain.</b>

92
00:06:26.666 --> 00:06:28.250
<b>But </b>

93
00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:30.458
<b>some out of friendship ,</b>

94
00:06:30.458 --> 00:06:35.750
<b>or without fully knowing the truth or</b>
<b>falsehood of the situation. </b>

95
00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:38.083
<b>participated in this war</b>

96
00:06:38.083 --> 00:06:44.791
<b>By doing so, they became party to sin</b>
<b>and also had to lose their lives.</b>

97
00:06:44.791 --> 00:06:48.250
<b>Supporting a friend</b>
<b>or acquaintance in wrongdoing </b>

98
00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:50.666
<b>is not a sign of being well-wishing. </b>

99
00:06:50.666 --> 00:06:54.000
<b>The mark of being well-wishing</b>
<b>is to make them understand, </b>

100
00:06:54.000 --> 00:07:00.458
<b>by at least not supporting them,</b>
<b>and trying to stop their misdeeds.</b>

101
00:07:00.458 --> 00:07:06.666
<b>Whenever you support someone,</b>

102
00:07:06.666 --> 00:07:09.375
<b>understanding right and wrong. </b>

103
00:07:09.375 --> 00:07:10.375
<b>Otherwise, </b>

104
00:07:10.375 --> 00:07:15.708
<b>the chances of your downfall,</b>
<b>like theirs, will increase.</b>

105
00:07:16.208 --> 00:07:19.875


106
00:07:19.875 --> 00:07:24.791
<b>Duryodhana is boosting the morale</b>
<b>of everyone in his army.</b>

107
00:07:24.791 --> 00:07:25.916
<b>If you also </b>

108
00:07:25.916 --> 00:07:30.958
<b>lead a team in any industry or organization, </b>

109
00:07:30.958 --> 00:07:34.583
<b>you can certainly learn here.</b>

110
00:07:34.583 --> 00:07:37.041
<b>It is necessary for a leader </b>

111
00:07:37.041 --> 00:07:41.666
<b>to keep encouraging every colleague, </b>

112
00:07:41.666 --> 00:07:45.500
<b>to keep making them aware of their importance. </b>

113
00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:49.750
<b>Their role in your plan may be small, </b>

114
00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:51.125
<b>but </b>

115
00:07:51.125 --> 00:07:53.958
<b>for them, this work is important; </b>

116
00:07:53.958 --> 00:07:57.250
<b>it's their identity.</b>

117
00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:01.500
<b>When you appreciate someone's skills </b>

118
00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.541
<b>and give importance to this identity of theirs, </b>

119
00:08:04.541 --> 00:08:10.166
<b>their respect for you automatically increases.</b>

120
00:08:10.166 --> 00:08:12.333
<b>Remember, </b>

121
00:08:12.333 --> 00:08:17.250
<b>every colleague is first a sensitive person</b>

122
00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:21.333
<b>for whom having respect for their leader </b>

123
00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:24.250
<b>is as necessary as their work.</b>

